    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6d7d7570_2cd6a7ee",
        "filename": "core/java/android/uwb/RangingSession.java",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 124,
      "author": {
        "id": 1355916
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-01-07T00:27:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Any thoughts on what values would be output when a session is being opened but not yet started?",
      "parentUuid": "44106f9d_2023cd31",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 124,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 124,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "d5bf4b39ede82a5ff0b1800df59585c176b2352f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2fed1815_4229b3f9",
        "filename": "core/java/android/uwb/RangingSession.java",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 124,
      "author": {
        "id": 1121403
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-01-07T02:14:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can send an empty Bundle as the sessionInfo when the session is opened, but not started. In the future, some protocols may need to send some sessionInfo before a session is started. Alternatively, we can have some synchronous query like RangingSession.getSessionInfo() -\u003e PersistableBundle, but we need to protect the data with mutex/synchronized blocks to prevent race conditions.",
      "parentUuid": "6d7d7570_2cd6a7ee",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 124,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 124,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "d5bf4b39ede82a5ff0b1800df59585c176b2352f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
